course: dictionary
lesson: 11200
title: Witness: seeing and telling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A witness is a person who sees something happen, especially an accident or a crime. As a verb, to witness something means to see it happen: «we witnessed a rainbow over the sea». Look at the clues around the word: a rainbow is something you see, so witnessed means saw it happen.
explain: In a court, a witness is a person who tells the court what they know or saw. Witnesses promise to tell «the whole truth», because leaving out important parts can mislead people too. «An honest witness tells the truth» is a good way to remember it.
explain: A witness can also be a person who watches someone sign an important paper, and then signs it too. An eyewitness is someone who saw an event with their own eyes. If you witness an accident, tell a grown-up or call for help.
fact: A witness is a person who sees something happen, especially an accident or a crime.
fact: As a verb, «witness» means to see something happen: «we witnessed a rainbow over the sea».
fact: In a court, a witness tells the court what they know or saw.
fact: An eyewitness is someone who saw an event with their own eyes.
fact: If you witness an accident, tell a grown-up or call for help.
exercise: «We witnessed a rainbow over the sea.» What does witnessed mean here? | Ran away from it | Painted a picture of it | Heard about it from a friend | *Saw it happen
exercise: In a story, detectives question the witnesses. Who are the witnesses? | The police cars parked outside | The judges who sit in court | *People who saw what happened | The detectives themselves
exercise: You witness an accident in the street. What should you do? | Walk away and say nothing | *Tell a grown-up or call for help | Take a photo and post it online | Wait to see if someone else deals with it
test: «The witness told the court what she saw on the bridge.» Who is the witness? | The lawyer who asked the questions | *The woman who saw what happened on the bridge | The bridge itself | The judge who sat at the front
test: Which word means a person who saw something with their own eyes? | *Eyewitness | Eyelash | Sunglasses | Spectacles
exam: When a witness promises to tell the whole truth in court, what do they promise? | *To tell what they know and leave out nothing important | To say nothing at all | To make up a story to help a friend | To tell only the parts they like
